Subject: [PATCH] bmcweb: clear invalid state directory in root mode

The root-mode service uses /home/root as its working directory and stores
bmcweb_persistent_data.json there when STATE_DIRECTORY is absent. systemd
already ignores the absolute StateDirectory=/home/root value. Generate an
empty directive instead, retaining the existing data path without migrating
sessions, system UUID or event subscriptions. Leave experimental dynamic-user
mode's valid StateDirectory=bmcweb configuration unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/config/meson.build
+++ b/config/meson.build
@@ -192,7 +192,10 @@
     user = 'root'
     group = 'root'
     dynamic_user = 'no'
-    state_directory = '/home/root'
+    # StateDirectory accepts names relative to /var/lib, not absolute paths.
+    # Keep legacy root-mode persistence in WorkingDirectory: persistent_data
+    # falls back to '.' when STATE_DIRECTORY is absent. Do not move old data.
+    state_directory = ''
     work_dir = '/home/root'
 endif
 
